          <text class="dmono-sm" x="652" y="232">root cause + evidence, across runs</text>

          <rect class="dbox" x="325" y="190" width="250" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dtext" x="341" y="214">Fix → coding agent</text>
          <text class="dmono-sm" x="341" y="232">claude code · cursor · copilot · codex</text>

          <rect class="b-entire" x="14" y="190" width="250" height="56"></rect>
          <text class="dtext t-entire" x="30" y="214">Commit → Entire checkpoint</text>
          <text class="dmono-sm t-entire" x="30" y="232">the fix keeps its reasoning</text>

          <g color="var(--ink-2)">
            <line class="darr" x1="264" y1="74" x2="319" y2="74" marker-end="url(#arw)"></line>
            <line class="darr" x1="575" y1="74" x2="630" y2="74" marker-end="url(#arw)"></line>
            <line class="darr" x1="761" y1="102" x2="761" y2="184" marker-end="url(#arw)"></line>
            <line class="darr" x1="630" y1="218" x2="575" y2="218" marker-end="url(#arw)"></line>
            <line class="darr" x1="319" y1="218" x2="264" y2="218" marker-end="url(#arw)"></line>
            <line class="darr" x1="139" y1="184" x2="139" y2="108" marker-end="url(#arw)"></line>
          </g>
          <text class="dmono-sm" x="750" y="147" text-anchor="end">grouped with</text>
          <text class="dmono-sm" x="750" y="162" text-anchor="end">related incidents</text>
          <text class="dmono-sm" x="152" y="139">next run verifies</text>
          <text class="dmono-sm" x="152" y="154">the detection</text>
          <text class="dmono-sm" x="152" y="169">stopped firing</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption><b>Neatlogs is built as a circuit, and Entire is the segment that makes it auditable.</b> The fix leaves Neatlogs as a prompt to a coding agent; that agent's session becomes a checkpoint; the next production run either clears the detection or doesn't. Demonstrating one full lap of this on video is the single highest-leverage thing you can record — it hits agent quality, tool use, and demo clarity at once.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="defs">
        <div>
          <dt>Traces &amp; spans</dt>
          <dd>Every LLM call, tool invocation, retrieval, rerank and guardrail check as a typed tree, with inputs, outputs, timing, tokens and cost.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Detections</dt>
          <dd>Rules evaluated against spans as they arrive; matches show as badges on the trace and in the span panel. Four types: <strong>regex</strong> over span text, <strong>condition</strong> over numeric attributes (tokens, latency, cost), <strong>PII</strong> scanning, and <strong>classifier</strong> for semantic category. Read-only post-processing — it never changes your app's behaviour.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Investigate</dt>
          <dd>Multi-step reasoning over your runs — comparative analysis across traces to isolate the real failure and its evidence, then an investigation report with a recommended fix and verification steps. Rationed by plan (3 on Free, 50 on Starter, unlimited on Pro).</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Evals</dt>
          <dd>Quality standards written in plain language, then scored automatically against runs at scale.</dd>
